  <page_number>316</page_number>
  <running_head>P. VOET</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Id-</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">justitiam. Adeoque duplici</l>
    <l n="2">afflictione contra divinum</l>
    <l n="3">textum oneraretur afflictus, &amp;</l>
    <l n="4">quod passus esset injuriam, &amp;</l>
    <l n="5">quod eam intulisset injuriam</l>
    <l n="6">homo pessimus impune. Quae</l>
    <l n="7">res cum abeat in contemptum</l>
    <l n="8">injuriati, eundem majori malo</l>
    <l n="9">mactabit. Ut nihil magis offi-</l>
    <l n="10">cio sit contrarium, quam ita</l>
    <l n="11">alium servare, ut alter damno</l>
    <l n="12">afficiatur. <i>Id enim esset &amp; impium</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>&amp; irrisorem justificare, &amp; justum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>impium facere, accipere personam</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>impii,&amp; declinare facere justum in</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>judicio.</i> Quae omnia Deo sunt</l>
    <l n="17">abominatio.</l>
    <l n="18" para="true">Neque etiam dicatur, æ-</l>
    <l n="19">quum non esse, ut propter rem</l>
    <l n="20">leviculam, id est, illaras[?] inju-</l>
    <l n="21">rias, fustibus, aut simili quo</l>
    <l n="22">instrumento, in injuriantes</l>
    <l n="23">animadvertatur. Quia, non a-</l>
    <l n="24">liter evitabitur hoc malum,</l>
    <l n="25">nisi ignominioso quo pœnæ</l>
    <l n="26">genere, tales puniantur.</l>
  </main_text>
  <marginalia>
    <note side="left" at="Ut nihil magis" line_from="9" line_to="9">l. si quis ex signa-tor. l), quemad. Testam. aperiant. l. sancti-mus. Cod Admin. Tutor. Proverb.</note>
    <note side="left" at="Quae omnia Deo" line_from="16" line_to="16">17. v.15.</note>
    <note side="left" at="Neque etiam dicatur," line_from="18" line_to="18">&amp; 18.</note>
    <note side="left" at="Neque etiam dicatur," line_from="18" line_to="18">v.5. Pho-eyl.</note>
    <note side="left" at="Neque etiam dicatur," line_from="18" line_to="18">Foem. Admo-nitorio.</note>
  </marginalia>
  <notes>The note block in the left margin is set in small type; its line breaks are reproduced in the note order given. "Admo-nitorio." keeps its printed hyphen. "illaras" is read as printed but is doubtful.</notes>
